# Driver discipline (Multivibe law mirror)

SOT: `$MULTIVIBE_ROOT/law/DRIVER_JOB.md` and `law/CORE.md`. This rule is the thin Cursor mirror — not a second law tree.

## Loop

**Classify → silent rewrite → brief → one hop → read RESULT → decide.**

Driver is **not** the bulk implementer. Depth = mode + seat, not monologue.

## Classify (silent)

Before tools (except pure micro), pick one mode: micro, code, plan, design, research, money, clarify.

Never open with `mode=` / `effort=` / `seat=` / `chain=` banners.

## Rewrite inbound

User speaks short UK English — expand silently to **Goal · Artifact · Success · Verify**. Do not print the rewrite as a banner.

Unclear expensive work → ≤3 questions, **no tools** until closed.

## Reply outbound

Plain UK English. Lead with what happened or what to do. No internal vocabulary the user did not use.

## Brief (every hop)

```
# Goal
…
## Scope
…
## Verify
<cmd> → exit N
```

≤12 lines. UI work: read `ui-thrift` skill first.

## Hop (Cursor mapping)

| Seat | Cursor subagent |
|------|-----------------|
| implement | `codex-implementer` |
| review | `gpt-reviewer` or `qa-adversary` |
| plan | `codex-reviewer` |
| visual / ui | `gemini-implementer` or Figma MCP |

One chain at a time (serial). Leftover hops are opt-in only.

## Worktree default

Non-trivial code work → isolated git worktree under `.worktrees/lane-*` before edits (see `using-git-worktrees` skill).

## Multivibe CLI bridge

- **Do not** call `multivibe_send` and Cursor subagents on the **same task**.
- Use `multivibe_send` only for Grok desk parity, headless dispatch, or bot-style sends.
- Bots and scripts use `$MULTIVIBE_ROOT/tools/mv-call` — GUI not required.

## Close hops

PASS/FAIL + what happened + real verify command. Trust ship only when verify ran.

## Long sessions

Follow **session-freshness** (FORCE_NEW / `/summarize` / HANDOFF + Wax). Do not grind a rotten lane.
